            "To enable Live Preview for your Next.js CSR (App Router) application, perform the following steps:",
            "Step 1: Install the @contentstack/live-preview-utils package via npm or yarn: npm install @contentstack/live-preview-utils",
            "Step 2: Initialize the Live Preview SDK on the client side. import { livePreview } from '@contentstack/live-preview-utils'; livePreview({ stack_details: { api_key: process.env.CONTENTSTACK_API_KEY, }, enable: true, host: process.env.CONTENTSTACK_API_HOST, });",
            "Step 3: Add live_preview config to your Contentstack Stack initialization on the server side. import contentstack from 'contentstack'; const Stack = contentstack.Stack({ api_key: process.env.CONTENTSTACK_API_KEY, delivery_token: process.env.CONTENTSTACK_DELIVERY_TOKEN, environment: process.env.CONTENTSTACK_ENVIRONMENT, live_preview: { preview_token: process.env.CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_TOKEN, enable: true, }, });",
            "Step 4: Use the onEntryChange callback to re-render your application with draft content when an entry is edited in the CMS. import { onEntryChange } from '@contentstack/live-preview-utils'; onEntryChange(() => { // Re-render your application with the updated draft content });"
